# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version determined by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: `app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing Analytics in the root layout

### 3. Implementation Details
- Fetched latest installation instructions from official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- Followed framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router
- The Analytics component integrates seamlessly with Next.js routing
- Component is placed at the end of the body tag as recommended by Vercel docs

### 4. Verification Steps Completed
✅ Package installed successfully using npm
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter passed with no issues
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes introduced

## Next Steps
To start collecting analytics data:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics tab → Enable button)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Analytics data will appear in the dashboard after users visit the site
4. Verify setup by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Technical Notes
- The `<Analytics />` component is a Next.js-optimized wrapper around the tracking script
- It provides automatic route tracking for Next.js navigation
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- Analytics will only activate when deployed to Vercel's platform
